# --- vendor/ is COMMITTED upstream source ---------------------------------
# Un-ignore it wholesale.  Two UNANCHORED rules above silently ate most of it:
#   `bin/`   matched vendor/2.11BSD/usr/bin
#   `*.bin`  matched vendor/2.11BSD/usr/usr.bin and vendor/netbsd-0-9/usr.bin
#            -- DIRECTORIES whose names end in .bin
# The first commit landed 841 of 2007 files, excluding every build input
# (sh, tcsh, elvis), and reported success.  tools/cleanroom.sh caught it by
# failing to build the shells from a fresh clone.
!vendor/
!vendor/**
# modplace.s -- GENERATED per module by tools/gen_modplace.py: this module's
# offset inside the shared module bank, derived from the MEASURED sizes of the
# modules placed before it.  Ignored for the same reason as kernel_exports.s
# beside it: it is a build product with no clean-checkout state, and tracking a
# file that every module-size change rewrites would conflict on every branch.
src/modules/*/modplace.s

